\title{Countable and countably infinite sets}
\date{2026-03-12T13:52:35Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A set #{A} is \em{countable} if it [has the same cardinality as](00AR) (\ie can be put into [bijection](00AF) with) a subset of #{\N}. Note that #{\N} is a subset of itself: in particular, we say #{A} is \em{countably infinite} if #{|A| = |\N|}.}
